  SETUP
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓  Collection 'multi_url' ready
  ✓  3 fixture URLs registered (no real HTTP)

  APPROACH COMPARISON
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Option A — three separate WEB.INGEST calls:
    source.execute_query({'op': 'WEB.INGEST', 'url': url1, ...})
    source.execute_query({'op': 'WEB.INGEST', 'url': url2, ...})
    source.execute_query({'op': 'WEB.INGEST', 'url': url3, ...})

  Option B — one WEB.INGEST call with urls list:
    source.execute_query({'op': 'WEB.INGEST', 'urls': [url1, url2, url3], ...})

  Both produce identical results. Use urls list for cleaner code when
  you have a batch of URLs ready at the same time.

